---
/**
 * /medical-devices - the first vertical page (ADR-0020 in the Trooth repo).
 *
 * Every licence, condition, quirk and key on this page is rendered from src/data/catalog.json,
 * which jobs/site_data.py copies verbatim out of catalog/sources/*.yaml. The held endpoints
 * come from registry.json with the reason each is held. Nothing about a source is typed here,
 * so the page cannot claim terms the catalog does not.
 *
 * No grades of our own (H2, ADR-0014). The benchmark slot is Modafied's hotlinked emblem.
 * Nothing on this page may describe the API in the present tense before Phase 1 ships.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Emblem from '../components/Emblem.astro';
import { MODAFIED_EMBED_SRC } from '../utils/modafied';
import { p } from '../utils/paths';
import catalog from '../data/catalog.json';
import registry from '../data/registry.json';

const DEVICE_IDS = [
  'openfda-device-510k',
  'openfda-device-pma',
  'openfda-device-classification',
  'openfda-device-recall',
  'openfda-device-enforcement',
  'openfda',
];
const HELD_IDS = ['fda-ai-enabled-devices', 'openfda-device-udi', 'openfda-drug-event', 'openfda-drug-enforcement'];

const byId = new Map((catalog.sources as any[]).map((s) => [s.id, s]));
const sources = DEVICE_IDS.map((id) => byId.get(id)).filter(Boolean) as any[];

const registryEntries = (registry.groups as any[]).flatMap((g) => g.entries ?? []);
const held = HELD_IDS.map((id) => registryEntries.find((e: any) => e.id === id)).filter(Boolean) as any[];

function keyOf(endpoint: any) {
  const k = endpoint.records?.key;
  return Array.isArray(k) ? k.join(' + ') : k;
}
---

<Layout
  title="Medical device data from FDA"
  description="FDA's device clearances, approvals, recalls, product codes and adverse event reports: what each feed holds, how they join, the licence read from FDA's own page, and the quirks that bite."
  activeNav="feeds"
>
  <section style="margin-bottom:2rem; max-width:820px;">
    <h1 style="font-size:2.25rem; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Medical device data from FDA</h1>
    <p style="font-size:1.1rem; color:var(--text-muted);">
      If you are building a medical device, or software that has to get through FDA, you need the
      regulatory record: what has been cleared, under which product code, what has been recalled,
      and what has gone wrong in the field. FDA publishes all of it for free through openFDA. It is
      spread across separate endpoints with different date formats, different identifiers and
      different refresh schedules, and nothing tells you how they fit together.
    </p>
    <p style="color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:0.75rem;">
      This page covers {sources.length} of those feeds. For each one the licence was read from
      FDA's own page, the record key was checked against live responses, and the quirks were
      found by fetching it. Trooth will route to them once the API ships (Phase 1); until then
      this page is the guide. Grades, where they exist, are Modafied's and are shown as Modafied
      publishes them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size:1.35rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.75rem;">How the feeds join</h2>
    <div style="overflow-x:auto;">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Identifier</th><th>Looks like</th><th>Links</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Product code</td><td><code>FMK</code></td><td>Classification is the table of codes. 510(k), PMA, recalls and adverse event reports all carry one.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>510(k) number</td><td><code>K262526</code></td><td>Clearance records, and the <code>k_numbers</code> list on a recall.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>PMA number + supplement</td><td><code>P150031 / S084</code></td><td>Approval records. Most rows are supplements, not new devices.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Recall number</td><td><code>Z-3133-2026</code></td><td>Called <code>product_res_number</code> in recalls and <code>recall_number</code> in enforcement reports. Same value.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>MDR report key</td><td><code>mdr_report_key</code></td><td>Adverse event reports. <code>report_number</code> is not unique; follow-ups reuse it.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p style="color:var(--text-muted); margin-top:0.75rem; max-width:820px;">
      One timing detail worth knowing before you build on recalls: a recall reaches the recall
      endpoint before it reaches the enforcement report. On 2026-09-22, Z-3139-2026 and
      Z-3140-2026 were in the first and not yet in the second.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size:1.35rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:1rem;">The feeds</h2>
    <div style="display:grid; gap:1rem;">
      {sources.map((s) => (
        <article class="card" id={s.id} style="padding:1.25rem 1.4rem;">
          <div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:1rem; flex-wrap:wrap; align-items:flex-start;">
            <div style="max-width:640px;">
              <h3 style="font-size:1.15rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.35rem;">{s.name}</h3>
              <p style="color:var(--text-muted); font-size:0.95rem;">{s.description}</p>
            </div>
            <Emblem subjectId={s.id} size="sm" />
          </div>

          <dl style="display:grid; grid-template-columns:max-content 1fr; gap:0.35rem 1rem; margin-top:1rem; font-size:0.9rem;">
            <dt style="color:var(--text-subtle);">Endpoint</dt>
            <dd>{s.endpoints.map((e: any) => <code style="margin-right:0.5rem;">{e.url}</code>)}</dd>
            <dt style="color:var(--text-subtle);">Record key</dt>
            <dd>{s.endpoints.map((e: any) => <code style="margin-right:0.5rem;">{keyOf(e)}</code>)}</dd>
            <dt style="color:var(--text-subtle);">Refreshes</dt>
            <dd>{s.refresh_cadence}</dd>
            <dt style="color:var(--text-subtle);">Licence</dt>
            <dd>
              <a href={s.license.url}>{s.license.spdx}</a>, read from FDA's page on {s.use_terms.confirmed_on}.
              Commercial use: {s.use_terms.commercial}. Redistribution: {s.use_terms.redistribution}.
            </dd>
            <dt style="color:var(--text-subtle);">Rate limit</dt>
            <dd>{s.cost.rate_limit}</dd>
          </dl>

          {s.quirks?.length > 0 && (
            <details style="margin-top:0.9rem;" open>
              <summary style="cursor:pointer; font-weight:600;">Quirks ({s.quirks.length})</summary>
              <ul style="margin:0.5rem 0 0 1.1rem; color:var(--text-muted); font-size:0.9rem; line-height:1.55;">
                {s.quirks.map((q: string) => <li>{q}</li>)}
              </ul>
            </details>
          )}

          <details style="margin-top:0.6rem;">
            <summary style="cursor:pointer; font-weight:600;">Licence conditions</summary>
            <ul style="margin:0.5rem 0 0 1.1rem; color:var(--text-muted); font-size:0.9rem; line-height:1.55;">
              {s.use_terms.conditions.map((c: string) => <li>{c}</li>)}
            </ul>
          </details>

          {s.denominator?.notes && (
            <details style="margin-top:0.6rem;">
              <summary style="cursor:pointer; font-weight:600;">What a count here does not tell you</summary>
              <p style="margin-top:0.5rem; color:var(--text-muted); font-size:0.9rem; line-height:1.55;">{s.denominator.notes}</p>
            </details>
          )}
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom:2.5rem; max-width:820px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:1.35rem; font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Not listed yet, and why</h2>
    <p style="color:var(--text-muted); margin-bottom:1rem;">
      These are useful and are not in the catalog, each for a stated reason. A feed with an open
      licence question stays out until the question is answered.
    </p>
    <div style="display:grid; gap:0.75rem;">
      {held.map((e) => (
        <div class="card" style="padding:0.9rem 1.1rem;">
          <div style="font-weight:700;"><a href={e.homepage}>{e.name}</a></div>
          <p style="color:var(--text-muted); font-size:0.9rem; margin-top:0.3rem;">{e.why}</p>
          <p style="color:var(--text-subtle); font-size:0.85rem; margin-top:0.3rem;">{e.notes}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom:2rem; max-width:820px;">
    <p style="color:var(--text-subtle); font-size:0.85rem;">
      FDA's notice, carried with every one of these feeds: do not rely on openFDA to make decisions
      regarding medical care; results are unvalidated. Nothing here implies FDA endorsement.
      See the <a href={p('/feeds')}>full feed directory</a> for every other source.
    </p>
  </section>

  <script is:inline defer src={MODAFIED_EMBED_SRC}></script>
</Layout>
